@{ slug="dodge"; name="Dodge"; nameAr="دودج"
   title="Dodge Repair &amp; Service Dubai | FixHive Garage"
   desc="Expert Dodge repair in Dubai. Charger, Challenger, Durango &amp; Dodge 1500 specialists. HEMI V8, SRT Hellcat &amp; Demon engine servicing. FixHive Garage Dubai."
   models="Charger · Challenger · Durango · RAM 1500 Classic · Durango SRT"
   heroSub="Dubai specialists for Dodge Charger, Challenger and Durango — 5.7L and 6.4L HEMI V8, SRT Hellcat supercharged and Widebody servicing."
   intro1="Dodge occupies a unique position in Dubai's automotive market — the brand of unapologetically American muscle, where the Charger and Challenger have loyal followings among enthusiasts who appreciate the combination of powerful V8 engines, rear-wheel drive and dramatic styling. The SRT models — Charger Hellcat, Challenger Hellcat and the 807-horsepower Challenger SRT Demon (a car that was never officially sold in the UAE but arrived via personal import) — are genuine performance icons with an active community of owners in Dubai and Abu Dhabi."
   intro2="The HEMI family covers the 5.7L (RT models), 6.4L 392 (Scat Pack and Durango SRT), and the 6.2L supercharged (Hellcat and Redeye). All use Multi-Displacement System (MDS) on the 5.7 and 6.4, requiring 0W-40 Chrysler MS-12633 oil. The Hellcat's supercharged 6.2L does not use MDS and is a more straightforward engine from a service perspective, but its supercharger drive belt and intercooler coolant are service items that standard 5.7 owners never encounter. The eight-speed ZF 8HP transmission serves all V8 Dodge models and is excellent but benefits from periodic fluid maintenance."
   intro3="Dubai's heat creates specific challenges for Dodge HEMI owners. The cars are often used enthusiastically — acceleration runs on empty evening roads, desert highway cruising — and these driving patterns combined with 45°C+ ambient temperatures place the cooling system, brake system and drivetrain under greater thermal stress than their American-market service intervals account for. FixHive provides complete Dodge HEMI service including supercharger service on Hellcat models, pre-track inspections and comprehensive diagnostic coverage."
   i1h="HEMI MDS Lifter Failure &amp; Engine Tick"
   i1p="The 5.7L and 6.4L HEMI's Multi-Displacement System uses collapsible lifters to deactivate four cylinders under light load. In UAE conditions — particularly with the short-trip pattern common in Dubai (AC pre-cooling, short drives to mall or restaurant, park for hours in heat) — the engine rarely reaches full operating temperature before shutdown, which prevents the oil from fully circulating through the MDS passages. This pattern, combined with any delay in oil changes, causes sludge in the MDS solenoid circuits and eventual lifter collapse. The characteristic 'HEMI tick' — a tapping noise from the engine — is the first symptom. We service the solenoids and replace lifters with the updated design or fit an MDS-delete kit for customers who prefer to disable the system."
   i2h="Hellcat Supercharger Drive Belt &amp; Intercooler"
   i2p="The 6.2L supercharged Hellcat engine uses a Roots-type positive displacement supercharger driven by a 6-rib accessory belt at approximately 2.3x crankshaft speed. In Dubai's heat, the supercharger inlet air temperature rises rapidly without the intercooler's chilled water system functioning correctly. The intercooler pump and its dedicated coolant reservoir are maintenance items that many independent workshops are unfamiliar with. The supercharger belt should be inspected every 30,000 km and replaced by 60,000 km — a belt failure on a running engine causes immediate catastrophic supercharger damage. We stock Hellcat supercharger belts and intercooler coolant."
   i3h="Brake Fade &amp; Rotor Warping Under UAE Conditions"
   i3p="Dodge's performance models — particularly the Challenger SRT and Durango SRT — are used enthusiastically by UAE owners who take advantage of Dubai's late-night traffic lull. Repeated hard braking from high speed causes brake rotor temperatures to reach glazing point on the standard cast-iron rotors. Rotor warping (producing a pulsating brake pedal) and pad glazing (reduced braking response despite pedal effort) are the consequences. We recommend upgrading to two-piece floating rotors on high-use Hellcat models and carry EBC Yellowstuff pads as a significant upgrade over stock for owners who regularly use their cars spiritedly."
   i4h="Rear Axle Seal Leaks &amp; Differential Service"
   i4p="The solid rear axle (8.25-inch and Dana 60 units) fitted to Dodge Charger and Challenger RWD models requires axle seal inspection at every major service. The axle seal gaskets are relatively simple components but in UAE conditions — where the car may sit in direct sunlight for hours at a time and the axle oil expands and contracts with heat cycles — seal degradation is accelerated. A leaking axle seal allows differential oil to coat the rear brakes and contaminate the brake pads, causing brake fade and eventually dangerous brake failure. We inspect and replace rear axle seals as preventive maintenance on all V8 Dodge models."
   faq1q="How much does Dodge HEMI servicing cost in Dubai?"
   faq1a="Minor Dodge V8 services at FixHive start from AED 450–600 covering oil change with 0W-40 MS-12633, filter, multi-point inspection and brake check. Major services every 30,000 km covering transmission fluid, differential service, spark plugs and supercharger belt inspection (Hellcat) range from AED 900–1,800."
   faq2q="What oil does a Dodge HEMI need in Dubai?"
   faq2a="5.7L and 6.4L HEMI engines require Chrysler MS-12633 0W-40 full synthetic. The 6.2L Hellcat uses the same specification. Never use 5W-20 or 5W-30 in a UAE-driven HEMI — the MDS system relies on the 0W-40 viscosity curve for correct solenoid oil pressure."
   faq3q="How often should I service a Dodge Challenger or Charger in Dubai?"
   faq3a="Oil changes every 8,000 km or annually. Transmission fluid (ZF Lifeguard 8) every 60,000 km. Differential oil every 40,000 km. Brake fluid annually. Supercharger belt inspection every 30,000 km (Hellcat). Air filter every 15,000 km."
   faq4q="Can FixHive service the Dodge Challenger Hellcat and SRT in Dubai?"
   faq4a="Yes. The Hellcat's 6.2L supercharged engine, intercooler system and wide-body brake package are all within our capability. We have serviced multiple Hellcats, Redeyes and a small number of Demons in the UAE."
   faq5q="What are common Dodge problems in Dubai?"
   faq5a="HEMI tick (MDS lifter wear), transmission torque converter shudder on overdue-service examples, rear axle seal leaks and brake rotor warping from enthusiastic use are the most common items on UAE Dodge vehicles."
   ctaSub="HEMI V8, Hellcat supercharger, ZF 8-speed and rear axle service — Dodge muscle car specialists in Dubai."
